// Title: Suspicious Dropbox API Usage
// Sigma ID: 25eabf56-22f0-4915-a1ed-056b8dae0a68
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-20 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, exfiltration, T1105, T1567.002
// Description: Detects an executable that isn't dropbox but communicates with the Dropbox API
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the API with a tool that the author wasn't aware of
// References:
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/7e906adc-9d11-447f-8641-5f40375ecebb
//   - https://www.zscaler.com/blogs/security-research/new-espionage-attack-molerats-apt-targeting-users-middle-east
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_domain_dropbox_api.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where (RemoteUrl endswith "api.dropboxapi.com" or RemoteUrl endswith "content.dropboxapi.com") and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\Dropbox"))
